  "summary": "I reconciled Walter Kim's (pt-0005) med list against the St. Brigid discharge summary and the signed addendum (10/19), following RBC-TOC-02. The addendum overrides the summary where they differ.\n\nChanges:\n- **Furosemide:** raised from 20 mg to 40 mg daily, on the 40 mg tablet. The old order was replaced by mr-t0001.\n- **Spironolactone:** started at 25 mg daily (mr-t0004). The discharge summary said 12.5 mg; the signed addendum corrects it to 25 mg.\n- **Potassium chloride:** stopped.\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg daily:** the held order was resumed rather than reordered. The discharge said to restart it once creatinine was below 1.5. The 10/21 outside lab shows creatinine 1.32 and potassium 4.4, so that condition is met.\n\nNo change:\n- **Metoprolol XL 50 mg:** another name for his existing metoprolol succinate 50 mg order.\n- **Atorvastatin and aspirin:** continued as before.\n- **Omeprazole:** kept. The pantoprazole was only the hospital's substitute for it, so I didn't order pantoprazole.\n\nNeeds your decision:\n- **Metoprolol tartrate 25 mg twice daily:** the discharge papers don't mention it, and it may double up with the metoprolol succinate. I left it unchanged and sent you a message (comm-t0005).\n\nFollow-up:\n- **Potassium/kidney lab:** the discharge asks for this test 1 week after starting spironolactone, around 10/26. I didn't order it because the hospital may already have. I created a task for you, due 10/26 (task-t0006), to make sure it gets done. His potassium needs watching now that he's on lisinopril and spironolactone together without the potassium supplement.\n- **Follow-up visit:** the discharge asks for a visit with us within 7 days (by 10/26), and none is on the schedule. This still needs booking.\n\nThe reconciliation is documented in a progress note (doc-t0007) that cites the source documents, the labs and the policy.",
